      ],
      "note": "Front elevation. Rubble masonry, paired and single white windows, acute arches on the southern first floor and individual gabled dormers. Central tower is scaffolded in this frame."
    },
    {
      "kind": "kartaview",
      "frame": "146585451",
      "walls": [
        13,
        14,
        15,
        16
      ],
      "note": "Projecting end has a stepped gable and narrow attic opening. Stone stringcourses run around the corner. Main approach climbs through the lawn."
    },
    {
      "kind": "kartaview",
      "frame": "146585439",
      "walls": [
        14,
        16,
        18,
        19,
        22
      ],
      "note": "Axial approach shows the tower projecting in front of the wings and the level difference to the drive."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.uwo.ca/fm/img/what_we_do/bldg/UH.jpg",
      "note": "Clear view without scaffolding. Top of the tower has paired open arches, battlements and taller corners. Repeated window pairs sit under gabled dormers."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.uwo.ca/visarts/research/2011-12/special_spaces/bk/Kestle2.jpg",
      "note": "Straight-on tower, recessed Gothic doorway and broad outdoor stair in flights with black rails."
    },
    {
      "kind": "aerial",
      "note": "City of London 2025 orthophoto. A broad level roof is edged by dark slopes with dormer and gable projections. The square tower sits on the east approach. A lower flat-roof north addition steps back to the west."
    },
    {
      "kind": "lidar",
      "note": "Inventory P50 15.46 m, P90 17.31 m, maximum 25.04 m. Main roof approximately 16–17 m. The north addition reads around 12 m. Tower peaks at approximately 25 m."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.uwo.ca/img/about/bnr/brescia-bnr.jpg",
      "walls": [
        14,
        16,
        18,
        19,
        22
      ],
      "note": "Campus panorama resolves six twin-window dormers, three on either side of the tower. Tall pointed chapel windows line the south wing, paired rectangular windows the north. The lawn-side flight reaches the tower portal. Sunlit masonry and portal stone sampled here."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.uwo.ca/img/about/bnr/brescia-bnr.jpg",
      "walls": [
        14,
        16,
        18,
        19,
        22
      ],
      "note": "The tower crown has a taller blunt corner shaft and cross. The six principal dormers sit at the slope edge on the east front."
    },
    {
      "kind": "aerial",
      "note": "Ursuline Hall has small flat north and south return roofs with light grey membrane and pale stone coping, with a paved forecourt beyond the south wall."
    }
